<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The audit separates model capacity from the memory module. ACT and Diffusion Policy are the base experts for the two TRACE interfaces, while the VLA baselines include their released adaptation paths and frozen components. The TRACE updater is shared across adapters, so the added capacity can be attributed to a fixed memory module plus a small policy-facing translator rather than to a new action backbone.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ A.2 Model Size and Hyperparameters ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendix ‣ TRACE: Trajectory-Routed Causal Memory for Delayed-Evidence Visuomotor Imitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> reports the additive parameter budget of TRACE for two policy-facing interfaces. The reference base expert is used only as the audited denominator for the percentage. The row name describes the TRACE interface rather than a fixed combined method. The added count includes the shared updater and the policy-specific adapter. The percentage is computed as <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100\times N_{\mathrm{added}}/N_{\mathrm{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>added</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>base</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100\times N_{\mathrm{added}}/N_{\mathrm{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> from the audited counts.</p>
</div>
