</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The added-parameter table shows that the two interfaces have different capacity costs because they condition different base experts. The regression interface adds <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12.69" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12.69</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12.69</annotation></semantics></math>M parameters over the audited ACT checkpoint, and the diffusion interface adds <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="27.94" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>27.94</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">27.94</annotation></semantics></math>M over the audited Diffusion Policy checkpoint. These counts are used for capacity accounting. They are not used as a substitute for the physical rollout comparisons in Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5 Empirical Evaluations ‣ TRACE: Trajectory-Routed Causal Memory for Delayed-Evidence Visuomotor Imitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
