</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The training table is intentionally separate from the architecture table below. Table <a href="#A1.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ A.2 Model Size and Hyperparameters ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendix ‣ TRACE: Trajectory-Routed Causal Memory for Delayed-Evidence Visuomotor Imitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> records the optimisation budget, action horizon, and fine-tuning choices used in the reported training protocol. Table <a href="#A1.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ A.4 State Representation and Normalisation ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendix ‣ TRACE: Trajectory-Routed Causal Memory for Delayed-Evidence Visuomotor Imitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> records the memory architecture values that determine the TRACE module size and routing interface.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Dataset and Demonstration Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ A.3 Dataset and Demonstration Details ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendix ‣ TRACE: Trajectory-Routed Causal Memory for Delayed-Evidence Visuomotor Imitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> makes the data accounting explicit for the five real robot tasks. The physical rollout count is the main evaluation count used in Equation <a href="#A1.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ A.1 Problem Setup Details ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendix ‣ TRACE: Trajectory-Routed Causal Memory for Delayed-Evidence Visuomotor Imitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>. Tool, Book, and Laundry counts and horizons are audited from the processed LeRobot metadata. Cable and Medicine counts and horizons are audited from the local ROS bag timestamp scan using the same <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30</annotation></semantics></math> Hz sampling rule as the converter.</p>
</div>
