</span></div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="A1.T14.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><sup id="A1.T14.3.1" class="ltx_sup">†</sup> Diffusion timing uses the shared measured TRACE path. Base forward is the 100-step diffusion denoising call.</p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS8.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS8.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The latency table shows that TRACE adds a small fixed computation before the unchanged base policy call. For the regression adapter, the overhead is visible because the base policy is already fast. For the diffusion adapter, the same memory path is small compared with the 100-step diffusion denoising call. The table therefore supports the claim that TRACE is an online conditioning module rather than a second policy pass or an offline retrieval procedure.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.9 </span>Memory Update, Training, and Online Inference</h3>

<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14551v1/train_inference_overview.png" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/248;" width="476" height="248" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Training and inference consistency. Training scans the masked fixed-budget history available online, and deployment applies the same updater once per executed step.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At each step, camera features are pooled as <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}=C^{-1}\sum_{c}\rho(f_{\mathrm{vis}}(o_{t}^{(c)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>vis</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}=C^{-1}\sum_{c}\rho(f_{\mathrm{vis}}(o_{t}^{(c)}))</annotation></semantics></math>, and the proprioceptive embedding is <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}=\phi_{s}(\tilde{s}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}=\phi_{s}(\tilde{s}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. These features form the visual-state content <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{t}=[v_{t},p_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{t}=[v_{t},p_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math>. The address feature <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is built from the projected path signature and delta signature. When first-frame anchoring is enabled, <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> also includes the causal first-frame anchor. With this address vector, the route query and write distribution are</p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{\rho}(q_{t}),\qquad\bar{m}_{t-1,k}=m_{t-1,k}+\lambda_{\eta}\eta_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{\rho}(q_{t}),\qquad\bar{m}_{t-1,k}=m_{t-1,k}+\lambda_{\eta}\eta_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell_{t,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell_{t,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{(W_{q}\rho_{t})^{\top}W_{k}\bar{m}_{t-1,k}}{\tau\sqrt{d_{r}}},\qquad\omega_{t,k}=\frac{\exp(\ell_{t,k})}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp(\ell_{t,j})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{(W_{q}\rho_{t})^{\top}W_{k}\bar{m}_{t-1,k}}{\tau\sqrt{d_{r}}},\qquad\omega_{t,k}=\frac{\exp(\ell_{t,k})}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp(\ell_{t,j})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed sinusoidal slot identity when enabled; setting <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\eta}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\eta}=0</annotation></semantics></math> gives the adapters that do not use slot identity. The content proposal, write strength, and slot update are</p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{w}(e_{t},q_{t})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{w}(e_{t},q_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{m}_{t,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{m}_{t,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tanh\!\left(\phi_{m}(\bar{m}_{t-1,k},u_{t},\rho_{t})\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.896em;" width="1.896em"><mi>tanh</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tanh\!\left(\phi_{m}(\bar{m}_{t-1,k},u_{t},\rho_{t})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{t,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{t,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\omega_{t,k}\sigma\!\left(\phi_{\beta}(\bar{m}_{t-1,k},u_{t},\rho_{t})\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\omega_{t,k}\sigma\!\left(\phi_{\beta}(\bar{m}_{t-1,k},u_{t},\rho_{t})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m_{t,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m_{t,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\beta_{t,k})m_{t-1,k}+\beta_{t,k}\tilde{m}_{t,k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\beta_{t,k})m_{t-1,k}+\beta_{t,k}\tilde{m}_{t,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The memory readout uses a separate attention distribution:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u_{t}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u_{t}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{r}(e_{t},\rho_{t})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{r}(e_{t},\rho_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{m}_{t,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{m}_{t,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=m_{t,k}+\lambda_{\eta}\eta_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=m_{t,k}+\lambda_{\eta}\eta_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{t,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{t,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{(u_{t}^{r})^{\top}W_{k}^{r}\bar{m}_{t,k}}{\sqrt{d}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{(u_{t}^{r})^{\top}W_{k}^{r}\bar{m}_{t,k}}{\sqrt{d}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{t,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{t,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(a_{t,k})}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp(a_{t,j})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(a_{t,k})}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp(a_{t,j})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z_{t}^{\mathrm{mem}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>mem</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z_{t}^{\mathrm{mem}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\alpha_{t,k}W_{v}^{r}m_{t,k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\alpha_{t,k}W_{v}^{r}m_{t,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">During training, each target time <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> uses a padded fixed-budget causal history index sequence <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{L,r}(t)=(i_{1},\ldots,i_{L})\subseteq\{1,\ldots,t\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{L,r}(t)=(i_{1},\ldots,i_{L})\subseteq\{1,\ldots,t\}</annotation></semantics></math> with valid mask <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>. The selected valid entries contain the first available frame, the current frame, and a recent stride-sampled tail. Starting from <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{(0)}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{(0)}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the scan is</p>
<table id="A1.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M^{(l)}=\mathcal{U}_{\theta}(M^{(l-1)},o_{i_{l}},s_{i_{l}},q_{i_{l}},b_{l}),\qquad l=1,\ldots,L." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{(l)}=\mathcal{U}_{\theta}(M^{(l-1)},o_{i_{l}},s_{i_{l}},q_{i_{l}},b_{l}),\qquad l=1,\ldots,L.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This scan applies the same updater that deployment uses once per online step with the cached memory state. The final scanned memory forms <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the native policy loss for expert family <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{policy}}^{(e)}=\mathbb{E}_{(\tau,t)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\ell_{e}\!\left(\mathcal{E}_{\psi}^{(e)}(x_{t},\mathcal{A}^{(e)}_{\theta}(H_{t})),y_{t}^{\star}\right)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>policy</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{policy}}^{(e)}=\mathbb{E}_{(\tau,t)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\ell_{e}\!\left(\mathcal{E}_{\psi}^{(e)}(x_{t},\mathcal{A}^{(e)}_{\theta}(H_{t})),y_{t}^{\star}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The finite-slot updater has three common failure modes during training. Slot collapse writes most evidence through a few slots. Diffuse writing spreads one observation across many slots, making later addresses weak. Read-write mismatch stores information in a form that the readout cannot recover after subsequent updates. TRACE uses one lightweight stabiliser for each case, then keeps the downstream imitation objective unchanged.</p>
<table id="A1.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{policy}}^{(e)}+\lambda_{\mathrm{bal}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{cons}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cons}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>policy</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>bal</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>bal</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>cons</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>cons</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{policy}}^{(e)}+\lambda_{\mathrm{bal}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{cons}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cons}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p2.4" class="ltx_p">For the <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th selected history element of target <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{t,l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{t,l}</annotation></semantics></math> be the slot-routing distribution, <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t,l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t,l}</annotation></semantics></math> the write proposal, and <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t,l}^{\mathrm{mem}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>mem</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t,l}^{\mathrm{mem}}</annotation></semantics></math> the memory readout. With <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{v}=\sum_{t,l}b_{t,l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{v}=\sum_{t,l}b_{t,l}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\omega}^{(j)}=N_{v}^{-1}\sum_{t,l}b_{t,l}\omega_{t,l}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\omega}^{(j)}=N_{v}^{-1}\sum_{t,l}b_{t,l}\omega_{t,l}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the auxiliary terms are</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>bal</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=K^{-1}\sum_{j=1}^{K}\left(\bar{\omega}^{(j)}-K^{-1}\right)^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=K^{-1}\sum_{j=1}^{K}\left(\bar{\omega}^{(j)}-K^{-1}\right)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E42.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(N_{v}\log K)^{-1}\sum_{t,l}b_{t,l}\left(-\sum_{j=1}^{K}\omega_{t,l}^{(j)}\log\omega_{t,l}^{(j)}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi>log</mi><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(N_{v}\log K)^{-1}\sum_{t,l}b_{t,l}\left(-\sum_{j=1}^{K}\omega_{t,l}^{(j)}\log\omega_{t,l}^{(j)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cons}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>cons</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cons}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=N_{v}^{-1}\sum_{t,l}b_{t,l}d^{-1}\left\|\tanh z_{t,l}^{\mathrm{mem}}-\tanh u_{t,l}\right\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>mem</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=N_{v}^{-1}\sum_{t,l}b_{t,l}d^{-1}\left\|\tanh z_{t,l}^{\mathrm{mem}}-\tanh u_{t,l}\right\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS9.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>bal</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}</annotation></semantics></math> penalises uneven average routing, so it discourages slot collapse. <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}</annotation></semantics></math> penalises high-entropy routing at each valid write step, so it discourages diffuse writing. <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cons}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>cons</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cons}}</annotation></semantics></math> aligns the bounded memory readout with the current write proposal, so it reduces read-write mismatch.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These terms are finite-capacity stabilisers rather than theoretical guarantees. They bias training toward balanced, addressable, and readable writes, but they do not prove that every piece of causal information remains recoverable. Since the memory has a fixed number of slots and a bounded slot width, sufficiently long horizons or trajectories with more pieces of information than the memory can represent may still force multiple facts to share capacity. In such regimes, later updates can overwrite or blur earlier content, especially when evidence is repeatedly routed to nearby slots or when visually similar observations require different interpretations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The auxiliary terms act only on memory. The downstream policy loss remains chunk L1 with the standard optional KL term for Regression, and the native diffusion denoising loss for Diffusion.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Causal TRACE memory update and adapter conditioning.</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            Observation <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, robot state <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, previous memory <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, previous signature <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, optional first-frame anchor <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, state mask <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, train-split normalisation statistics, policy family <math id="alg1.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\{\mathrm{regression},\mathrm{diffusion}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>regression</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>diffusion</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\{\mathrm{regression},\mathrm{diffusion}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            Updated memory <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, signature <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, adapter conditioning <math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and policy prediction <math id="alg1.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            Apply the task mask and state normalisation.

<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}_{t}=Z_{q}(s_{t}),\qquad\tilde{s}_{t}=(\bar{s}_{t}-\mu_{s})/(\sigma_{s}+\epsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}_{t}=Z_{q}(s_{t}),\qquad\tilde{s}_{t}=(\bar{s}_{t}-\mu_{s})/(\sigma_{s}+\epsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
            Append <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to the piecewise linear history path <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
            Compute <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t}=\operatorname{Sig}_{\leq p}(S_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Sig</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t}=\operatorname{Sig}_{\leq p}(S_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}=\xi_{t}-\xi_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}=\xi_{t}-\xi_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
            Remove the scalar signature coordinate, standardise <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, then map them to <math id="alg1.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}=\phi_{g}(\xi_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}=\phi_{g}(\xi_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta g_{t}=\phi_{\Delta}(\delta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta g_{t}=\phi_{\Delta}(\delta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
            Encode the current observation as <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}=C^{-1}\sum_{c}\rho(f_{\mathrm{vis}}(o_{t}^{(c)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>vis</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}=C^{-1}\sum_{c}\rho(f_{\mathrm{vis}}(o_{t}^{(c)}))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}=\phi_{s}(\tilde{s}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}=\phi_{s}(\tilde{s}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
            Compute address features <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}=[g_{t},\Delta g_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}=[g_{t},\Delta g_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math>, appending <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> only when first-frame anchor routing is enabled, and set <math id="alg1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}=\phi_{\rho}(q_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}=\phi_{\rho}(q_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
            Route the write with Equation <a href="#A1.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ A.9 Memory Update, Training, and Online Inference ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendix ‣ TRACE: Trajectory-Routed Causal Memory for Delayed-Evidence Visuomotor Imitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
            Form gated write candidates from visual-state content and address state, then update slots with Equation <a href="#A1.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ A.9 Memory Update, Training, and Online Inference ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendix ‣ TRACE: Trajectory-Routed Causal Memory for Delayed-Evidence Visuomotor Imitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
            Read memory with Equation <a href="#A1.E37" title="Equation 37 ‣ A.9 Memory Update, Training, and Online Inference ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendix ‣ TRACE: Trajectory-Routed Causal Memory for Delayed-Evidence Visuomotor Imitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
            Construct <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}=(M_{t},z_{t}^{\mathrm{mem}},g_{t},\Delta g_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>mem</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}=(M_{t},z_{t}^{\mathrm{mem}},g_{t},\Delta g_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}^{(e)}=\mathcal{A}_{\theta}^{(e)}(H_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}^{(e)}=\mathcal{A}_{\theta}^{(e)}(H_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
            Predict <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{t}=f_{\psi}(z_{t},c_{t}^{(e)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{t}=f_{\psi}(z_{t},c_{t}^{(e)})</annotation></semantics></math> with the unchanged base policy.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.10 </span>Additional Case Studies</h3>

<div id="A1.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T15" title="Table 15 ‣ A.10 Additional Case Studies ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendix ‣ TRACE: Trajectory-Routed Causal Memory for Delayed-Evidence Visuomotor Imitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> summarises the concrete delayed-evidence structure behind the five tasks. These case studies connect the diagnostic quantities in the main paper to rollout-level behaviour and give the evidence source for the baseline failure patterns discussed in the main text.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T15" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 15: </span>Additional task-level case studies linking baseline failures, evidence, and TRACE behaviour.</figcaption>
<div id="A1.T15.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:448.9pt;vertical-align:-222.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-11.0pt,14.3pt) scale(0.940054495912807,0.940054495912807) ;">
<table id="A1.T15.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T15.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T15.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.5pt 2.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T15.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:31.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T15.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Task</span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T15.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.5pt 2.0pt;">
